<aura:component implements="force:appHostable,flexipage:availableForAllPageTypes,flexipage:availableForRecordHome,force:hasRecordId,forceCommunity:availableForAllPageTypes,lightning:actionOverride,force:lightningQuickActionWithoutHeader">
    
Create Budget:
•	Enter the mandatory required information (marked with an asterisk) *:
•	Budget Name is a free text field, it is recommended you follow a naming convention for easy identification. Eg. “RMF Budget for Amazon Q1 2021” 
•	Description and Comments are optional fields, available to capture notes and comments.
•	Program is search look up field, one must type in first few letter of the program name, before making a selection
•	Budget Partner is search look up field, one must type in first few letter of the account name, before making a selection
•	Budget Reduction Amount is used to decrease amount from an existing budget, this can be left blank when creating a new budget
•	Budget Amount is the amount of funds being allocated to the account for the said budget period
•	Start Date defines start of the budget period
•	End Date defines end of the budget period
•	Budget Type is applicable to the RMF program, there are 2 budget types to choose from RSA MD and Retail MDF

Key Points:
•	Once the budget is created it is set to pending review requiring approval from a finance manager
•	Duplicate or overlapping budgets cannot be created. Duplicate/Overlapping budget is one that has the same Budget Partner, Budget Type and same/overlapping start and end dates


On the approve budget page include the following in the app guidance 

Approve/Reject Budget:

In order to approve/reject a budget
1.	Review budget details 
2.	Navigate to the “Related” tab
3.	On the Approval History table, click on Approve/Reject buttons to record review decision
4.	Enter comments and save decision

	
</aura:component>